			<Component name="ObservationLocator" CardinalityMin="0" CardinalityMax="1">
				<Documentation>Component for the data property assertions that specify where exactly an Observation is located or appears in the Source where it was extracted from.</Documentation>
				<Element name="pageScanUrl" ConceptLink="http://data.tastade.org/ontology/pageScanUrl" ValueScheme="string" CardinalityMin="1" CardinalityMax="0" cue:DisplayPriority="1" xmlns:cue="http://www.clarin.eu/cmd/cues/1">
					<Documentation>This is the link to the specific page (image/scan inside a source's folder) where an observation occurs.</Documentation>
				</Element>
				<Element name="locator" ConceptLink="http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/locator" ValueScheme="string" CardinalityMin="1" CardinalityMax="1" cue:DisplayPriority="2" xmlns:cue="http://www.clarin.eu/cmd/cues/1">
					<Documentation>An indication of a page, folio, line, or any other pointer to the specific part in a source where the observation occurs. If you entered the page Url above, here you could enter the page number as a label/string. PiCo says: "The position defines the order in which scans are presented on the web. This feature is required when a Source has multiple scans."</Documentation>
